  "body_html": "<h1>Value Of A Zero-Sum Game</h1>\n<p>For a finite matrix game, the maxmin and minmax coincide\n(<a class=\"node-ref\" data-node-id=\"zero_sum.von_neumann_minimax\" href=\"zero_sum_von_neumann_minimax.html\">Von Neumann Minimax Theorem</a>); the common scalar is the <strong>value</strong>\nof the game:\n$$\n  \\operatorname{val}(A) = \\underline v = \\overline v.\n$$</p>\n<p>The Lean development defines <code>MatrixGame.value := A.maximin</code> and provides\n<code>value_eq_maximin</code> (definitional) and <code>value_eq_minimax</code> (via the minimax\ntheorem).</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Def. 2.2.5] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>, <code>references/MechDesign.pdf</code>. A zero-sum game has a value when maxmin equals minmax.</li>\n</ul>",
  "proof_html": null,
